{
  "slug": "artist:lil-b",
  "name": "Lil B",
  "editorial_article": "Born Brandon Christopher McCartney in Berkeley, California, on August 17, 1989, Lil B first gained attention as a member of the hyphy-era hip hop group The Pack. The group's 2006 single 'Vans' became a surprise hit and their only appearance on the Billboard Hot 100. As a solo artist, McCartney pioneered 'cloud rap' and coined the term 'based,' defining it as a positive and bold lifestyle. His 2011 album 'I'm Gay (I'm Happy)' peaked at number 56 on the Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums chart. Across an expansive discography, he has explored diverse genres from comedy hip-hop to jazz, including the 2022 release 'Afrikantis.' His influential internet-based career has inspired numerous artists, including Kendrick Lamar, Tyler, the Creator, and Young Thug. Beyond music, he has gained notoriety for public feuds with NBA stars like Kevin Durant and James Harden, often playfully claiming to place them under a 'Based God curse.'",
